---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Callout from '@/components/ui/Callout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Paralegal Portfolio">
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent font-semibold">About</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl mt-4">
        Paralegal-grade work, AI-augmented method.
      </h1>

      <div class="prose prose-neutral mt-8 max-w-none">
        <p class="text-lg">
          This portfolio demonstrates that an AI-augmented operator can produce the full
          range of paralegal and legal-assistant work product at staff-paralegal quality —
          from intake memos through trial-prep binders, across six different practice areas.
        </p>

        <h2>The method</h2>
        <p>
          Every artifact on this site is produced through a hybrid workflow: AI handles the
          heavy lifting of drafting, formatting, and cross-referencing while a human operator
          (David Ruiz, Top Virtual PH) makes the strategic calls — what theory of the case to
          pursue, what tone to set in correspondence, where the facts cut differently than they
          first appear.
        </p>

        <p>
          On every artifact you'll find a <strong>"How this was made"</strong> disclosure
          panel. It names the AI method used, the points where human judgment was the
          deciding factor, and an honest comparison of the time taken versus a traditional
          unaided workflow.
        </p>

        <h2>Why fictional cases</h2>
        <p>
          Real client work belongs to clients. To demonstrate the same range of work product
          without ever using a real matter, this portfolio is built on six fictional
          California cases — fact patterns, parties, courts, and case numbers all invented.
          Every artifact carries a fictional-content stripe so it cannot be mistaken for real
          legal filing or advice.
        </p>

        <h2>Who this is for</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>U.S. attorneys and law-firm hiring managers</strong> evaluating outsourced
            paralegal support — to see exactly what tasks can be delegated and at what
            quality.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Paralegal students and legal VAs</strong> studying real-feeling artifacts
            in a no-stakes environment.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Other AI-augmented operators</strong> looking at how the disclosure
            pattern is applied, end-to-end.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <Callout tone="warn" title="Not legal advice">
        Nothing on this site is legal advice. All cases, parties, courts, and documents are
        fictional. Do not rely on any artifact here for the disposition of an actual matter.
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
